net: Let requests keep their connections to themselves

An embedder sometimes needs a request that neither takes a pooled
connection nor leaves one behind for others: retrying a request on a
new connection, or a "no keep-alive" setting. //net has no such
option; closing idle connections is session-wide and races with other
requests.

Every socket pool, HTTP/2 and QUIC session key and TLS session cache
key contains the request's ProxyChain, and ProxyChain carries opaque
data reserved for embedders that takes part in its comparison. So give
a URLRequest a connection partition: it travels in HttpRequestInfo and
StreamRequestInfo, and the JobController puts it as opaque data into
every proxy chain it resolves for the request. Requests of a partition
then get connections, sessions and TLS sessions of their own.

HttpNetworkSession::CloseConnectionPartition() closes a partition's
idle sockets, HTTP/2 and QUIC sessions once its requests are gone. It
also deletes socket pools of partitions that are no longer used:
ClientSocketPoolManagerImpl creates a pool per proxy chain and keeps it
for the life of the session, so a partition per request would leak one
pool each.

